eNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Arch Manning leads game-winning drive as Texas stuns LSU","description":"Arch Manning found Raleek Brown for a 4-yard touchdown pass along the left sideline with 3 seconds left as Texas escaped Tiger Stadium with a victory over LSU","published":"2026-11-15T13:13:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50487515/arch-manning-leads-game-winning-drive-texas-stuns-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5076950/kelley-jones","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelley_Jones_(American_football)"},"pick":{"pick":17,"round":1,"team":"SEA","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Kelley Jones (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelley_Jones_(American_football)","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:20Z","intro":"Kelley Maurice Jones (born March 11, 2004) is an American college football cornerback for the Mississippi State Bulldogs.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Jones attended Clarksdale High School in Clarksdale, Mississippi, where he played both defensive back and quarterback. As a senior, he passed for 558 yards with 10 touchdowns and rushed for 1,424 yards with 19 touchdowns. He committed to Mississippi State University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Jones played in three games and redshirted his first year at Mississippi State in 2023. As a redshirt freshman in 2024, he started four of 11 games and had 29 tackles. Jones entered his redshirt sophomore year in 2025 as a starter."}]}}